      "content": "i hear what u saying about \"perceived neglect\" but that feels like a way to avoid the actual substance. people aren't just \"feeling uncertain,\" they're seeing things happen in real time that the news refuses to cover. if u look at the actual grievances—like the way the system is being rigged or the loss of national identity—don't u think it's more than just \"emotional language\"? isn't there a core of truth in what they're saying that the \"neutral\" experts are just too scared to acknowledge?",
